            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Divine revelation, authority, and active communication, often representing God's power, presence, or the guidance of the Holy Spirit.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Psalm 29:3-9\",\"John 10:27\",\"Hebrews 3:7-8\",\"Genesis 3:8\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"A human herald or prophetic messenger preparing the way for the Lord, specifically typified by John the Baptist.\",\"basis\":[\"Isaiah 40:3\",\"John 1:23\",\"Mark 1:3\"],\"prominence\":\"dominant\"},{\"meaning\":\"The gentle, inward, and intimate guidance of God or the Holy Spirit.\",\"basis\":[\"1 Kings 19:12\",\"Isaiah 30:21\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Overwhelming divine judgment, majesty, and absolute, irresistible power.\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 1:15\",\"Ezekiel 43:2\",\"Joel 3:16\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"In biblical symbolism, 'voice' (especially the voice of the Lord) bridges the gap between God's transcendent power and His immanent relationship with creation. It can manifest as a universe-shattering force, a gentle whisper, or the prophetic calling of a human messenger.\"}",
